 ## Overview
-NRFF is a method for encoding view-dependent specular effects in neural radiance fields by replacing standard positional encodings and roughness parameters with Anisotropic Spherical Gaussians (ASG) and a custom Rendering Equation Encoding (REE) [S1]. It distinguishes itself from Ref-NeRF by using multiscale tensor decomposition for spatial representation and predicting ASG features to model complex reflections, rather than relying on isotropic roughness or precomputed environment maps [S1].
+NRFF is a method for encoding view-dependent effects in radiance fields by replacing the standard positional encoding and roughness/IDE inputs of Ref-NeRF with a structured latent representation of specular reflections [S1]. It differs from its siblings by explicitly modeling anisotropic reflections using Anisotropic Spherical Gaussians (ASG) and a custom Rendering Equation Encoding (REE) in the latent space, rather than relying on isotropic roughness or precomputed environment maps [S1].
 
